This Express rate-limit counter loses increments under concurrency because the read and write are separated by an await. Start from exactly this middleware:

const hits = new Map();
async function limiter(req, res, next) {
  const key = req.ip;
  const n = hits.get(key) || 0;
  await recordMetric(key, n); // async gap
  hits.set(key, n + 1);
  if (n + 1 > 100) return res.status(429).json({error:'rate_limited'});
  next();
}

Write a test that drives 200 overlapping requests (recordMetric awaits setImmediate) and proves the counter ends below 200. Then fix it by making the increment synchronous before any await, and keep the same test asserting the count reaches exactly 200 and request 101+ get 429. node --test must pass.

